{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993791602390001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"soar-shove-link","assignee":"","author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":5},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"Related operational cleanup: the sole live `unbound_jira` binding drift the canary was (correctly) trying to alert on was REB-532 — a leftover experiment issue ('EXPERIMENT (delete me): assignee clobber repro', empty rebar-id: label, no local binding). Deleted it in Jira via acli; the drift clears on the next reconciler snapshot refresh. This is why the canary saw drift all day (and thus exercised the failing rebar create write path). The .env-id fix (Gerrit change 285) is the durable fix for any future drift.","timestamp":1783188608643661001}],"created_at":1783188270082901001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe `Reconciler Heartbeat Canary` workflow (`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml`)\nfails on every run whenever `bridge-fsck` reports binding drift, because its\n`Open binding-drift alert` step calls `rebar create` (a write) but the store was\nnever write-initialized in CI — so the write seam rejects it.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n1. In a fresh checkout, mount the tickets branch with a bare\n   `git worktree add -B tickets .tickets-tracker origin/tickets` (as the canary does)\n   — this does NOT create `.tickets-tracker/.env-id`.\n2. Run any rebar write, e.g. `rebar create bug \"x\"`.\n\n- **Expected:** the write succeeds and a ticket is created.\n- **Actual:** `Error: ticket system not initialized. Run 'ticket init' first.` (exit 1),\n  raised by the write seam at `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py:180`, which refuses to\n  append any event unless `.tickets-tracker/.env-id` exists. `.env-id` is git-ignored,\n  never committed to the `tickets` branch, and is created only by `rebar init`.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe canary's `Mount tickets branch as a worktree` step does a bare `git worktree add`\nand never runs `rebar init`, so `.env-id` is absent. It was latent until the\nbinding-drift alerting step (commit `dc01c11fe`) added the first `rebar create` the\ncanary actually exercises; it fires whenever `bridge-fsck` sees drift. The documented\nheadless-CI provisioning path (`docs/architecture.md`) is `rebar init` — idempotent,\nnon-interactive, attaches to the existing `origin/tickets`, and seeds `.env-id`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A `rebar init` step is added to `reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` after the store is\n      mounted and rebar is installed, so `.env-id` is seeded before any rebar write.\n- [ ] The canary's `rebar create` / `rebar comment` / `rebar transition` write steps no\n      longer fail with \"ticket system not initialized\".\n- [ ] The step is idempotent and non-interactive (safe on every scheduled run).\n- [ ] Change is pushed to Gerrit `refs/for/main` with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7bb66a58-1fec-4f7d-9361-dd539283d577","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"73cb-2716-bde1-4655","ticket_type":"bug","title":"canary: rebar create fails 'ticket system not initialized' — mount step never seeds .env-id","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1182e291-2da0-43f4-a83c-f7da2594200c","8ffe39ab-ba8b-4b9c-83be-be4c96d506fa","7bb66a58-1fec-4f7d-9361-dd539283d577","3c8b87a1-e24c-451f-ae06-627377c13bf1","b976736e-6889-4f07-976d-e64c17a1f9d2","26914c49-f1dc-4034-a06f-ac5412b43481"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993791602390001,"uuid":"674ffe39-ac2e-47b2-b34a-2ac91721e41f"}